    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d374">

                <pb facs="0520" n="432" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg432"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 860c.20/9</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bliss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of the Commission to
                        Negotiate Peace</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-01-23">January 23,
                            1919</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my letter of the 17th
                    instant, concerning the recruiting in the United States for the Polish Army, and
                    to your acknowledgment thereof, I beg to inform you that the Polish National <pb
                        facs="0521" n="433" xml:id="pg433"/> Committee notified me in a letter from
                    the Chief of the Military Department of that Committee, that the recruitment
                    referred to would be stopped on February 15th. I thereupon had another interview
                    with Mr. Dmowski, President of the Polish Committee in which I pointed out the
                    advisability that the recruitment be discontinued forthwith. He replied that he
                    would again take up the matter in council with the members of the Committee, and
                    I am glad to inform you that on again communicating with him to-day he has
                    informed me that a decision has been taken by the Committee to at once order the
                    discontinuance of further recruitment in the United States.</p>
                <p>I have requested Mr. Dmowski to inform me whether the necessary instructions to
                    this effect have been sent to the representative of Poland in the United States
                    and I will not fail to inform you of his answer.</p>
                <p>In accordance with the desire expressed in your letter of January 13th relating
                    to this same matter, I return herewith the enclosures which you forwarded at
                    that time.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Woods Bliss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
